course: dictionary
lesson: 6881
title: Opinion words: overrate
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: To overrate something is to think it is better or more important than it really is. Overrate is a verb: overrate, overrates, overrated, overrating. Its opposite is underrate, which means to think something is worse than it really is.
explain: Overrated is also an adjective, meaning not as good as people say. Read the clues around it: «That film is overrated.» If lots of people rave about a film but you find it only average, you might call it overrated. Because it is an opinion, you should always give a reason.
explain: Writers use these words in reviews and discussions. Look at this sentence: «The famous story that spinach's iron was overrated because of a misplaced decimal point is itself disputed and partly a myth.» The clue is disputed and partly a myth. The story itself is doubted, so a popular belief can be questioned.
fact: Overrate is a verb: overrate, overrates, overrated, overrating.
fact: «Overrated» can be an adjective meaning not as good as people say.
fact: Overrate means to think something is better than it really is. Underrate is its opposite.
fact: Overrated shows disagreement with popular opinion, so it is an opinion word and you should give reasons.
fact: In «The famous story that spinach's iron was overrated because of a misplaced decimal point is itself disputed and partly a myth», the word disputed means people argue about whether it is true.
exercise: «That band is overrated.» What does this mean? | It is brand new and nobody knows it yet | It is better than people say | It only plays music from the past | *It is not as good as people say
exercise: Which word is the opposite of overrate? | Rate | Praise | Overrating | *Underrate
exercise: Nadia says, «That film is overrated.» What should she add to make her opinion strong? | Say it again more loudly | *A reason, such as the plot being predictable | Stop talking about the film | Ask someone else to decide for her
test: In «The famous story ... is itself disputed and partly a myth», what does disputed mean? | It is a very old song | It is written in a book | *People argue about whether it is true | Everyone agrees it is true
test: Which sentence uses overrated correctly? | *Many people praise that book, but I think it is overrated | The sun is overrated because it is very hot | The rain is overrated since it falls down | I overrated my lunch, so I ate it all
exam: Which sentence gives an opinion and a reason? | The book is blue | *That book is overrated because the ending is predictable | I read the book yesterday | That book is overrated
